  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather with above normal temperatures \nthrough the weekend under high pressure.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nThe ridge of high pressure will keep winds light, skies mostly \nclear and temperatures above normal through the weekend. Highs \nwill be in the low to mid 80s this weekend for inland locations,\nand cooler along the coast with a sea breeze developing each \nafternoon. Cannot rule out early morning patchy river valley \nfog with radiational cooling. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Potential for a system moving in mid next week,\nbringing another round of wetting rainfall.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure lingers over the region this weekend, as a low \npressure system slides off the east coast early next week. \nGenerally, low pressure east of the Carolinas moves northeast in\nthe Atlantic, east of Nova Scotia. To the north, another low \npressure over Canada moves eastward, with a cold front that will\napproach our region Monday but likely stall before reaching us.\nMeanwhile, low pressure over the Great Lakes region will move \neast towards the area early next week bringing the greatest\nchance for wetting rain between Tuesday night and Thursday. Some\nthunderstorms are also possible with this system. Ensembles\ncurrently show a 50-60% chance of at least 0.5\" of rainfall.",
